# Cross-nursery INLINE-BODY send (M:N / --parallel ONLY) — regression guard for the routing leak.
#
# The outer `parallel:` spawns sibling O (recvs t, prints) and then calls inner(), whose nested
# nursery join EARLY-ENLISTS the outer nursery (O) into the one global MnSched. AFTER inner() returns,
# the OUTER BODY itself does `t.send(42)` — a send issued on the inline builder VM (self.mn == None,
# the sched held only in mn_enlist_sched). The wake of the enlisted, parked receiver O must route
# through that held sched; otherwise the value is queued but O is never made runnable → a false
# `deadlock` fault (or hang) under --parallel even though coop would print "O got 42".
#
#   chezzi run --parallel examples/parallel_cross_nursery_inline_send.chz   # → inner ran / O got 42 / done
#
# Output order: "inner ran" flushes at inner's nested join (during the body, before the send); O's
# output is buffered to its outer-nursery scope and flushes at the outer join, before "done".
#
# NOTE: `--parallel` is an accepted no-op alias — M:N is the only engine, so plain `run` succeeds too.
fn inner():
    spawn:
        print("inner ran")

fn main():
    t := Channel[int]()
    parallel:                        # OUTER nursery
        spawn:                       # O: child of OUTER — parks on recv until the inline body sends
            x := t.recv()
            print("O got {x}")
        inner()                      # nested nursery join → early-enlists OUTER (seeds O)
        t.send(42)                   # INLINE-BODY send — must wake the enlisted, parked O

    print("done")

main()
